# Assembled at build time by the platform's pipeline from jtk/content/*.json.
# A build artifact that happens to sit at the repository root; a stale copy in
# git is a second answer to "what does this site say".
jtk-content.json

# An entry's pictures, downloaded beside the entry at build time: a picture in
# a post's body is markdown — `![alt](media/<site>/<hash>.jpg)` — resolved
# relative to the file, so the build puts the file exactly where the body says.
jtk/content/**/media/


# The dev session's watch key (jtkit session): the page reads the platform's
# half through it. One session's, read-only, dead with the session — and not
# in git all the same.
jtk/session.json

# Where this copy stands on jtakeit (jtk push / jtk pull): the sha it was last
# brought to. A machine's position, not the site's; the kit never sends it.
.jtakeit/code.json

# The media library's pictures, on this machine (jtakeit-core wiki/108 §6). A
# picture a field names lives in the site's library, by its key; its file here
# is a copy — downloaded by `jtk media pull`, `jtk pull` or the dev server, or
# kept by `jtk media push` — and the build downloads its own. A second copy in
# git would be a second answer to "what does this site show".
src/assets/media/
# What `jtk media push` moved out of src/assets once the library held it and
# no code named it — never deleted, never committed; and the library's index.
.jtakeit/adopted/
.jtakeit/media.json
